# Scope for the `cargo tauri dev` watcher that scripts/tauri-dev.sh runs over
# crates/lucidos-app.
#
# This is an allow-list: ignore everything, then re-include what the Rust app
# compiles from. The TS frontend shares src/ with the Rust code, and the engine
# serves frontend changes from dist/ (ADR 0014), so a frontend edit must never
# restart the window. build.rs writes VERSION and .version_stamp into the crate,
# and tauri-build writes gen/, so those must stay ignored or a build retriggers
# itself. Folders under src/ stay ignored too, so a new TS folder restarts
# nothing. Entitlements.plist is left out: only `cargo tauri build` reads it.
#
# Tauri's watcher reads this file, never .gitignore, when it filters change
# events. The path crates the app depends on are watched in full, because
# tauri-cli finds them through `cargo metadata`.
# Plan: docs/plans/2026-09-25-tauri-dev-window-rebuilds-on-app-changes.md
#
# It lives here, one level up, because tauri-cli also tests the watched folder
# itself against the file. Inside the crate, `/*` matches the crate root's own
# empty relative path, so the whole crate would go unwatched.
/lucidos-app/*
!/lucidos-app/Cargo.toml
!/lucidos-app/build.rs
!/lucidos-app/tauri.conf.json
!/lucidos-app/Info.plist
!/lucidos-app/capabilities/
!/lucidos-app/permissions/
!/lucidos-app/icons/
!/lucidos-app/src/
/lucidos-app/src/**
!/lucidos-app/src/**/*.rs
